{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Cold iron shackles, ball and chain,
[F]Listen to the whistle of the [G]evenin' [C]train.
[C]You know you bound to [Dm7]wind up [C]dead,[C7]
[F]If you don't head back to [G]Tennessee [C]Jed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Rich man step on my poor head,
When you get back you better butter my bread.
Well, do you know it's like I said,
You better head back to Tennessee Jed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental}
[Bb] [F] [G] [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Tennessee, Tennessee, there [C]ain't no place [G]I'd rather [F]be,
[C]Baby won't you [G]carry [F]me [C]back to [G][F]Tennessee.[G][C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Drink all day and rock all night,
The law come to get you if you don't walk right
Got a letter this morning, baby all it read,
You better head back to Tennessee Jed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
I dropped four flights and cracked my spine,
Honey, come quick with the iodine,
Catch a few winks, baby, under the bed
Then you head back to Tennessee Jed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I run into Charlie Fog,
Blacked my eye and he kicked my dog,
My doggie turned to me and he said,
Let's head back to Tennessee Jed.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
I woke up a-feelin' mean,
I went down to play the slot machine,
The wheels turned around, and the letters read,
You better head back to Tennessee Jed.
{end_of_verse}
